      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 Asian Pacific Society of Respirology.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "BACKGROUND AND OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Cold-induced airway hyperresponsiveness (CAH) is common in bronchial asthma (BA) patients and represents a problem for those living in cold climate. Transient receptor potential melastatin 8 (TRPM8) channel is the main cold temperature sensor in humans that could mediate cold response in asthmatics with CAH. No associations between TRPM8 gene polymorphisms and CAH have been reported."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "METHODS",
            "content": "The present study involved 123 BA patients. CAH was assessed by 3-min isocapnic (5% CO2 ) cold air (-20°C) hyperventilation challenge. The c.750G\u2009>\u2009C (rs11562975), c.1256G\u2009>\u2009A (rs7593557), c.3048C\u2009>\u2009T (rs11563208) and c.3174C\u2009>\u2009G (rs11563071) polymorphisms of TRPM8 gene were genotyped by allele-specific polymerase chain reaction (PCR) and PCR with subsequent restriction fragment length polymorphism analysis."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "GC genotype and C allele carriers of the c.750G\u2009>\u2009C (rs11562975) polymorphism were more frequently observed to exhibit CAH. The estimated odds ratio for the GC genotype was 3.73 95%CI (1.48; 9.37), P\u2009=\u20090.005. Furthermore, GC heterozygotes had a prominent decrease in forced expiratory volume in 1\u2009s after the challenge as compared to GG homozygotes (-12% (-16; -8.1) vs -6.45% (-11; -2.1), P\u2009<\u20090.001). GC carriers also had a marked reduction in other spirometric parameters."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "The GC variant of the TRPM8:c.750G\u2009>\u2009C (rs11562975) polymorphism is associated with CAH in patients with BA, which suggests a potential role of TRPM8 in CAH development."
          }
        ]
      },
